    "number": "Theorem 3.1",
    "quote": "Given any set $\\B$ of $K$ bandits, time-horizon $T$, rounds $B$, parameters $q = T^{1/B}$ and $\\tau = 1$, the expected regret of \\pcomp \\ for the batched $K$-armed dueling bandits problem under the Condorcet assumption is at most $$ \\E[R(T)] \\leq 3KT^{1/B} \\log\\left(6TK^2B\\right) \\sum_{j: \\epsilon_{j} > 0} \\frac{1}{\\epsilon_{j}}.$$"
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Uses at most B batches. Regret defined via gaps eps, so pseudo-regret. Theorem 1.1 is the informal restatement."
  },
